Do not share the model file's mmap fd with NNAPI drivers.

With mmap sharing, the NNAPI delegate passes the mmapped model file's
descriptor to the driver inside the compilation request. Our models
live on external storage (fuse), which vendor HAL processes are not
allowed to read: on the Pixel 9 Pro the kernel's binder SELinux hook
rejects transferring the fd (avc denied { read } for dev="fuse"
scontext=u:r:hal_neuralnetworks_darwinn), getSupportedOperations fails
with FAILED_TRANSACTION, and the whole graph silently falls back to
CPU. Compile out only the weights-from-mmap branch so those operand
values are copied instead; TFLITE_NNAPI_ALLOW_MMAP_SHARING itself must
stay defined because it also guards NNMemory, the delegate's ashmem
input/output pools, without which the delegate cannot apply at all.

--- a/tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate.cc
@@ -1999,7 +1999,11 @@
                 nn_model_, ann_tensor_index, new_tensor->data.data,
                 new_tensor->bytes),
             "setting new operand value", tensor, nnapi_errno_);
-#ifdef TFLITE_NNAPI_ALLOW_MMAP_SHARING
+// Do not pass the mmapped model file's fd to the driver: our models
+// live on external storage (fuse), which vendor HAL processes may not
+// read, so the kernel's binder SELinux hook rejects the fd transfer
+// and delegation falls back to CPU.
+#if 0
       } else if (tensor->allocation &&
                  static_cast<const Allocation*>(tensor->allocation)->type() ==
                      Allocation::Type::kMMap) {
